# Hook Tooling Policy

RULE: Use `prek` (pre-commit wrapper) for all git hook management. Config in `.pre-commit-config.yaml`.
WHY: Consistent hook execution across all repos; prek normalizes pre-commit behavior and supports workspace-level config.
CODEX: 06-coding-standards/quality-gates.md

DO:
  prek install                              # after updating .pre-commit-config.yaml
  pre-commit install --install-hooks       # legacy repos only (without prek)
  Use pre-commit-hooks v6+ for new repos

NEVER:
  Custom shell scripts in .git/hooks/ (not portable, not tracked)
  pre-commit install without --install-hooks (hooks won't run until triggered)
  Mix prek and raw pre-commit in the same repo
  Older pre-commit-hooks versions unless repo-specific constraint requires it
